<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Stocks calm in first 1997 session.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Stocks calm in first 1997 session.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks remained quiet during the first after-hours trading session of 1997, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Not much is going on,&quot; said one of them.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one had a volume totalling 668,800 shares against 1,079,000 on December 31.</p>
<p>Session two had 241,400 shares compared to 3,468,512 on Tuesday.</p>
